    <section class="level" id="level-1" aria-labelledby="level-1-title">
      <header class="level-head">
        <div class="level-index" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
        <div>
          <p class="level-kicker">Level one · 第一级</p>
          <h2 id="level-1-title">For a 3-Year-Old <span lang="zh-CN">写给3岁孩子</span></h2>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="bilingual">
        <article class="panel panel-en" lang="en">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="lang-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="lang-label">English</span>
            <span class="panel-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <p>The sky is blue because sunlight is full of colors, and the tiny air all around us likes to bounce the blue light around the most.</p>
          <p>So when you look up, your eyes see all that blue light bouncing toward you from every direction. That makes the whole sky look blue!</p>
          <p>At sunset, the sunlight travels a longer way through the air, so most of the blue gets bounced away before it reaches you. Then you see orange and red instead.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="panel panel-zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="lang-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
            <span class="panel-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <p>天空是蓝色的，因为阳光里有很多种颜色，而我们周围的空气非常喜欢把蓝色的光弹来弹去。</p>
          <p>所以当你抬头看时，你的眼睛会看到从四面八方弹向你的蓝色光。于是整片天空看起来就是蓝色的！</p>
          <p>日落时，阳光要穿过更厚的大气层，大部分蓝光在到达你之前就被弹走了。这时你看到的就是橙色和红色。</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="level" id="level-2" aria-labelledby="level-2-title">
      <header class="level-head">
        <div class="level-index" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
        <div>
          <p class="level-kicker">Level two · 第二级</p>
          <h2 id="level-2-title">For a High School Teenager <span lang="zh-CN">写给高中生</span></h2>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="bilingual">
        <article class="panel panel-en" lang="en">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="lang-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="lang-label">English</span>
            <span class="panel-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <p>Sunlight looks white, but it is actually a mixture of all the colors of the rainbow. When sunlight enters Earth’s atmosphere, it collides with molecules of nitrogen and oxygen, which are much smaller than the wavelength of visible light.</p>
          <p>This causes a process called <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>. The molecules scatter shorter wavelengths much more strongly than longer ones—roughly in proportion to <span class="inline-math">1/λ<sup>4</sup></span>, where λ is the wavelength. Blue light has a shorter wavelength than red light, so it is scattered much more efficiently.</p>
          <p>During the day, scattered blue light reaches your eyes from all parts of the sky, so the sky appears blue. Violet light is scattered even more, but the Sun emits less violet, some of it is absorbed in the upper atmosphere, and our eyes are less sensitive to violet. The mix we perceive is therefore blue.</p>
          <p>At sunrise and sunset, sunlight passes through a much thicker layer of atmosphere. Most of the blue light is scattered out of the direct beam, leaving the longer orange and red wavelengths to reach your eyes.</p>
          <p>The sky is not blue because it reflects the ocean. It is blue because air molecules scatter sunlight.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="panel panel-zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="lang-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
            <span class="panel-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <p>阳光看起来是白色的，其实它是彩虹所有颜色的混合。当阳光进入地球大气层时，会与氮气和氧气分子碰撞，而这些分子比可见光的波长小得多。</p>
          <p>这会产生一种叫做<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的过程。分子对较短波长的散射比对长波长的散射强得多——大致与 <span class="inline-math">1/λ<sup>4</sup></span> 成正比，其中 λ 是波长。蓝光的波长比红光短，因此被散射的效率高得多。</p>
          <p>白天，散射的蓝光从天空的各个部分进入你的眼睛，所以天空看起来是蓝色的。紫光被散射得甚至更强，但太阳发出的紫光较少，一部分紫光被高层大气吸收，而且我们的眼睛对紫光也不够敏感。因此，我们感知到的混合颜色是蓝色。</p>
          <p>日出和日落时，阳光要穿过厚得多的大气层。大部分蓝光被散射出直射光束，只剩下较长的橙色和红色波长到达你的眼睛。</p>
          <p>天空呈蓝色并不是因为它反射了海洋。它呈蓝色是因为空气分子散射了阳光。</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="level" id="level-3" aria-labelledby="level-3-title">
      <header class="level-head">
        <div class="level-index" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
        <div>
          <p class="level-kicker">Level three · 第三级</p>
          <h2 id="level-3-title">For a Physics PhD <span lang="zh-CN">写给物理学博士</span></h2>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="bilingual">
        <article class="panel panel-en" lang="en">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="lang-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="lang-label">English</span>
            <span class="panel-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <p>The daytime sky’s blue color is primarily a consequence of <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> of solar radiation by density fluctuations in the atmosphere. For particles much smaller than the wavelength of light, the differential scattering cross-section varies approximately as
            <span class="formula" role="math" aria-label="d sigma over d Omega is proportional to one over lambda to the fourth power">dσ/dΩ ∝ 1/λ<sup>4</sup></span>
            for a fixed scattering angle, with the full angular dependence given by the Rayleigh phase function. In air, the relevant scatterers are molecules and short-lived clusters whose polarizability anisotropy and number density determine the scattering coefficient. The strong λ<sup>−4</sup> dependence means that blue photons (around 450 nm) are scattered several times more efficiently than red photons (around 650 nm).</p>
          <p>The observed sky radiance is not simply the single-scattering spectrum. It results from radiative transfer through an optically thin but multiply scattering medium, illuminated by the solar spectrum and viewed against a dark background. The incident solar spectral irradiance, ozone and other trace-gas absorption in the ultraviolet and visible, and the spectral response of human cone photoreceptors all shape the perceived color. Although violet light is scattered more strongly than blue, the solar spectrum has less violet power, atmospheric absorption suppresses part of it, and the eye’s sensitivity is lower at violet wavelengths; combined with chromatic adaptation and color-opponency processing, this yields the familiar blue percept rather than a violet sky.</p>
          <p>At low solar elevations, the optical path length through the atmosphere increases, and preferential extinction of short wavelengths by Rayleigh scattering reddens the direct solar beam. Aerosols and clouds add Mie scattering and can strongly modify both the color and polarization of the sky. Thus, the blue sky is best understood as a wavelength-dependent scattering and radiative-transfer phenomenon, with its perceived hue additionally conditioned by the solar spectrum, atmospheric absorption, and human visual processing.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="panel panel-zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="lang-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
            <span class="panel-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <p>白天天空的蓝色主要是太阳辐射被大气中密度涨落<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的结果。对于远小于光波长的粒子，微分散射截面近似满足
            <span class="formula" role="math" aria-label="d sigma over d Omega is proportional to one over lambda to the fourth power">dσ/dΩ ∝ 1/λ<sup>4</sup></span>
            （在固定散射角下），完整的角依赖关系由瑞利相函数给出。在空气中，相关的散射体是分子及短寿命团簇，其极化率各向异性和数密度决定散射系数。强烈的 λ<sup>−4</sup> 依赖意味着蓝光光子（约450 nm）的散射效率比红光光子（约650 nm）高数倍。</p>
          <p>观测到的天空辐亮度并不只是单次散射光谱。它是在光学薄但多次散射的介质中，经太阳光谱照明并以暗背景为衬托的辐射传输结果。入射太阳光谱辐照度、臭氧及其他痕量气体在紫外和可见光波段的吸收，以及人眼视锥细胞的光谱响应，共同塑造了感知到的颜色。虽然紫光比蓝光散射得更强，但太阳光谱中紫光功率较少，大气吸收抑制了其中一部分，而且眼睛对紫光波长的敏感度较低；再结合色适应和颜色拮抗处理，最终产生的是熟悉的蓝色感觉，而不是紫色天空。</p>
          <p>当太阳高度角较低时，穿过大气层的光程增加，短波长的瑞利散射优先消光，使直射太阳光束变红。气溶胶和云会引入米氏散射，并能强烈改变天空的颜色和偏振。因此，蓝天的本质最好理解为一种波长相关的散射与辐射传输现象，而其感知色调还取决于太阳光谱、大气吸收和人眼视觉处理。</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

